@host = https://localhost:7001/api/v1

### 1. Login -> 201 with accessToken, expiresAt, refreshToken, refreshExpiresAt
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grantType": "password", "email": "admin@okolariet.dk", "password": "YourSeedPassword1!" }

### 2. Protected endpoint with the token -> 200 (without the header -> 401)
GET {{host}}/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 3. Refresh -> 201, new pair
# @name refresh
POST {{host}}/auth/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grantType": "refresh_token", "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

### 4. Reuse the FIRST refresh token -> 401, and the login is now revoked
POST {{host}}/auth/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grantType": "refresh_token", "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

### 5. The new token from step 3 now also fails -> 401
POST {{host}}/auth/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grantType": "refresh_token", "refreshToken": "{{refresh.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

### 6. Missing field for the grant type -> 400
POST {{host}}/auth/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grantType": "password", "email": "admin@okolariet.dk" }

### 7. Log out (log in again first, steps 4-5 revoked the login) -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/auth/tokens/current
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
